# This file contains spyglass LINT and CDC waivers
# They were generated for design configuration "pbuf_3qs_axi" on Mon Nov 20 09:34:29 GMT 2017


# Waivers for lint_rtl goal ..
  waive -rule "STARC05-2.11.3.1" -msg "Combinational and sequential parts of an FSM described in same always block" -comment "All of these are fine. Most are just counters where the combinatorial part is ensuring the counter cannot rollover.  There are a couple of state machines here where nxt state has been rolled in with sequential process. Could change RTL but there is greater risk in changing the code"
  waive -rule "W164b" -msg "*LHS*" -comment " LHS has less bits than the RHS operand because in reality the RHS is the result of an operation itself. What the tool doesn't recognise is that the number of bits required to get the result of an operation is also depending on the maximum values assumed by the operands."
  waive -rule "W216" -msg "Inappropriate range select for*" -comment "We have to use these bit selects on the integers to avoid other LINT issues. Waived."
  waive -rule "W240" -msg "Input*declared but not read*" -comment "The design is configurable and certain parts of the code are only present in certain configurations. We use generates for this. Unfortunately, ports cannot be removed when using generates. Doesnt cause a real issue so this is Waived."
  waive -rule "W162" -msg "Extension of bits in constant integer conversion is erroneous*" -comment "This file converts some verilog defines in parameters. According to the value of the defines the value is representable with a variable number of bits, while for us the parameter has to have a fixed number of bits, so in some cases a zero-extension will happen, but this is not an issue at all and it can be waived."

