# Waivers for cdc_verify_struct goal ..
waive -rule "Ac_glitch03" -msg "*" -comment "Created by fmalaspi: flop meta can glitch and actually it's likely to be metastable, but it's ok because is the first flop of a synchronizer, so it's normal"
waive -rule "Ac_unsync02" -msg "Unsynchronized Crossing: destination flop gem.i_gem_ss.i_gem_top.i_gem_reg_top.i_gem_registers.prdata_i*, clocked by gem.pclk, source flop gem.i_gem_ss.i_gem_top.\gen_dma.gen_pbuf_axi_dma.i_edma_pbuf_axi_top .i_edma_pbuf_axi_fe.i_edma_pbuf_axi_fe_tx.db2_descr_ptr*" -comment "Created by ewanm.  Dont usually waive CDC paths, but this one is is ually put in the SGDC as a cdc_false_path. the only reason we dont is because of the / character in the path as a result of verilog generate. The waiver is as follows... The following is a path from the TX DMA to gem_registers. Specifically its the current descriptor pointer that becomes readable in gem_registers. The path is from aclk/hclk to pclk and is not synchronized. The reason is that it would only usually be read when the descriptor pointer is static, for debug reasons only. It doesn not need to be read for nrmal operation. Synchronizing it would consume a large number of flops and it has been decided it is not worth adding"
waive -rule "Ac_coherency06" -msg "*tx_start_pclk*synchronized twice*" -comment "Created by ewanm.  Dont usually waive CDC paths, but in this case we are not going to modify RTL to remove one of the synchronizers. Thy are for different blocks, both of which are optionally added through config options. Not related."
waive -rule "SGDC_cdc_false_path07" -msg "*from_type or to_type*" -comment "Created by ewanm.  Cant see anything wrong with the cdc_false_path constraint. from and to are given."
waive -rule "Ac_conv04" -msg "*prdata*" -comment "Created by ewanm. lots of sources feeding prdata for status and stats. Waived."
waive -rule "Ac_conv04" -msg "*two bits*axi_top*" -comment "Created by ewanm. This is because num_pkts_xfer is widened to house multiple queues, but each queue is actually independent."
waive -rule "Ac_conv04" -msg "*Control dest*pfc*" -comment "Created by ewanm. This is not grey encoded. Just using a sync flop multipled up. Tool misinterpreted code"
waive -rule "Ac_conv04" -msg "*Control dest*meta[*:*" -comment "Created by ewanm. This is not grey encoded. Just using a sync flop multipled up. Tool misinterpreted code"

