waive -rule "Ac_datahold01a" -msg "Synchronized crossing*db2_descr_ptr*sequencing check*" -comment "These are debug only and are only expected to work when the rest of the design is not active. Waived." 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*Partially-Proved*" -comment "None of these have failed, it is just the formal engine got to an appropriate depth of checking and stopped. we can assume these have passed due to the large formal depth. Waived." 
waive -rule "Ac_conv01" -msg "*Partially-Proved*" -comment "None of these have failed, it is just the formal engine got to an appropriate depth of checking and stopped. we can assume these have passed due to the large formal depth. Waived." 
waive -rule "Ac_conv04" -msg "*Partially-Proved*" -comment "None of these have failed, it is just the formal engine got to an appropriate depth of checking and stopped. we can assume these have passed due to the large formal depth. Waived." 
waive -rule "Ac_datahold01a" -msg "*Partially-Proved*" -comment "None of these have failed, it is just the formal engine got to an appropriate depth of checking and stopped. we can assume these have passed due to the large formal depth. Waived." 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*axi_xaction*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "This is status, to allow the user to identify busy times on AXI bus. if for the highly unlikely case that the axi xaction is high for less than 1 pclk cycle, it does not matter if the destination does not sample it high. Waived" 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*tx_dma_go*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "This is status, for debug only and does not matter if the source does not sample it high. Waived." 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*Fast*to slow*lockup_detect*" -comment "these are expected to stay high until software disables either the RX/TX or the lockup detect functionality. Waived." 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*dma_descr_ptr_tog*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "This is status to allow the user to identify what the current HW descriptor pointer is. If it toggles in short succession, it really doesnt matter as it is only a guidleine and is for debug only." 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*disable_tx*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "This signal is set when a major error event has occured. In order for it to be missed, 2 major events will need to have occured in close succession. This is not going to happen in a real system" 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*tsu_sec_incr*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "This event occurs set when the TSU timer increments past second intervals. Two of these events happening in less than 1 pclk cycle is not going to happen in a properly configured system" 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*timer_strobe*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "This event occurs set when the user sets gem_tsu_ms and gem_tsu_inc_ctrl in a way to cause the TSU time to be sampled into the strobe registers. Two of these events happening in less than 1 pclk cycle is not going to happen in a properly configured system" 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*tsu_timer_cmp*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "This event occurs set when the TSU timer meets the programmed cmp time. Two of these events happening in less than 1 pclk cycle is not going to happen in a properly configured system" 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*sync_gatestate*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "The formal engine in spyglass can reprogram the TSU such that it causes the gatestate to open and close within a tx_clk cycle, thus causing this CDC violation. Not going to happen in a properly configured system" 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*gen_tx_fifo_interface*i_cdnsdru_datasync_v1_tsu_hold*Data hold check:*FAILED*" -comment "The formal engine in spyglass can reprogram the TSU registers such that it races through all the ENST states ultra quick thus causing the tsu_hold signal to go high and low quickly thus causing this CDC violation. Not going to happen in a properly configured system" 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*i_gem_mmsl*i_sync_p_active_rx*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "The formal engine in spyglass can reprogram the TSU registers such that it races through all the ENST states ultra quick thus causing the tsu_hold signal to go high and low quickly thus causing this CDC violation. Not going to happen in a properly configured system" 
waive -rule "Ac_cdc01a" -msg "*gem_mac*rx_dv_bp*to*cdnsdru_datasync_v1_rx_dv.meta*Data hold check:FAILED" -comment "The tool reports rx_clk as slow clock and tx_clock as fast and this is not true because in this configuration the clocks have the same frequency. In general, however, the rx_clk can be the half frequency of tx_clk but no Data hold check can fail as the rx_dv_bp signal cannot change that fast, so thi can be waived." 
waive -rule "Ac_conv02" -msg "*i_sync_fsm_active*converge on combinational gate*i_enst_fc.n_state*Gray encoding check:*FAILED*" -comment "So basically after the reset, when the enst gets enabled, the gatestate goes down (default value) and fsm_active goes high. This does not constitute a problem in the destination clock domain as fsm_active is not racing with the gatestate signal. Indeed only if fsm_active is high then the destination clock domain FSM will start to work, and only then the gatestate signal will then be considered." 
